1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:25,000
CedarBridge C5 MCP Toolkit
Data reads. Action records. Orchestration verifies then records.

2
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:45,000
The host contains the agent and the MCP client.
The FastMCP server runs as a separate Python process.

3
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The client discovers schemas over stdio.
The OpenAI model selects a tool; the SDK invokes it through MCP.

4
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Exactly three registered tools.
These names come from the running server's actual discovery response.

5
00:01:30,000 --> 00:02:00,000
DATA: Project Clarity costs $15 for 30 minutes online.
The store still contains zero records.

6
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:25,000
ACTION: An explicit follow-up request creates a real local record.
The tool returns its committed record ID.

7
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:45,000
The read-only database query confirms one saved row.
No appointment is booked and no email is sent.

8
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:10,000
ORCHESTRATION: Look up Team Sprint, then record the interest.
The result shows the actual ordered capability outcomes.

9
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:35,000
One outer MCP call coordinates two internal Python capabilities.
The database now contains two records.

10
00:03:35,000 --> 00:04:10,000
FAILURE: Moon Camp is unknown.
Lookup failure stops the write. Record count remains two.

11
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:45,000
RETRY: The same email and service return the existing ID.
Atomic database uniqueness prevents duplicate rows across server runs.

12
00:04:45,000 --> 00:05:05,000
An informational question does not authorize saving contact details.
The Data tool remains read-only.

13
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:20,000
An invalid email triggers clarification in this live scenario.
Separate protocol tests prove server-side rejection too.

14
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:40,000
33 automated tests passed.
Real OpenAI checks and scripted-model SDK tests are labeled separately.

15
00:05:40,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Challenges: safe retries, precise result interpretation and Windows file closure.
Constraints, live checks and a regression test addressed them.

16
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:20,000
The repository includes source, research, setup, tests and reflection.
Future work: authenticated consent, retention and structured final answers.
